## Context
`scripts/doifetch.sh` pins DOIfetch at `DOIFETCH_REF` (its PR 1). Its raid f9e483
(DOIfetch session, 2026-10-29, through the inter-project protocol) is changing what
the harness documents in `skills/zotero/references/backfill.md` (about lines 150-164):

- DOIfetch 0011: an invalid ISBN is rejected (ValueError, nonzero exit) before any fetch.
  The backfill doc reads every nonzero exit other than 127/69 as "not found in the open
  sources", which would misreport a bad identifier.
- DOIfetch 0006: entry point moves to `doifetch.cli:main`; the `doifetch` console name stays.
- DOIfetch 0008: dispatch rewritten; public API `from doifetch import Request, Result, fetch`.
- DOIfetch 0013: OpenAlex joins the default cascade after Unpaywall, so the doc's default
  source list (Crossref, Unpaywall, HAL, ISTEX, EZproxy) goes stale.
- DOIfetch 0012 (DOAB) is out of that raid (DOAB REST API returns 403); not in this bump.

When: after DOIfetch 0008 merges. Author ruling (relayed by the DOIfetch session,
2026-10-29): DOIfetch goes 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0 with a signed tag `v0.2.0`, signed by the
author; pin that tag, not 0008's merge commit. The DOIfetch session announces the tag.

Further author rulings that change what the docs say:
- 0008 replaces `requests` with the standard library: the default install has no
  third-party dependency.
- 0012 reshaped: an ISBN is fetched by looking up the book's DOI on Crossref, then
  running the open-access DOI sources. LibGen becomes opt-in only (the harness still
  never passes it).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `DOIFETCH_REF` in `scripts/doifetch.sh` points at the tag `v0.2.0` (annotated, unsigned: author ruling 2026-10-29)
- [ ] `skills/zotero/references/backfill.md` lists the default sources of that ref
- [ ] The backfill doc tells an invalid-identifier exit apart from "not found", per the exit codes that ref emits
- [ ] One real `scripts/doifetch.sh --doi <open-access DOI>` run at the new ref downloads a PDF
